cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please credit the repository and Samuel C. Lange
  (The Chinese University of Hong Kong), and cite the survey papers for the
  lenses you use (see README.md).
type: dataset
title: "HST lens image reduction"
abstract: >-
  Hubble Space Telescope imaging of 133 galaxy-scale strong gravitational
  lenses from the SLACS, BELLS, BELLS GALLERY, SL2S and Project Dinos samples,
  reduced from the MAST archive into ready-to-model cutouts: science images,
  noise maps, PSF kernels with uncertainty maps, hand-drawn masks and
  hand-marked multiple-image positions, together with the pipeline that
  produces them.
authors:
  - family-names: Lange
    given-names: Samuel C.
    affiliation: The Chinese University of Hong Kong
repository-code: "https://github.com/samlange04/HST_lenses_data_reduction"
url: "https://github.com/samlange04/HST_lenses_data_reduction"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - strong gravitational lensing
  - Hubble Space Telescope
  - data reduction
  - drizzle
  - SLACS
  - BELLS
  - SL2S
date-released: "2026-10-25"
